      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1.1 Basic Profile"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Tripura is a small state in northeast India, surrounded by Bangladesh on three sides — north, south, and west — making it one of the most uniquely positioned states in India. It shares a land border of approximately 856 km with Bangladesh, which is significantly longer than its border with other Indian states. To the east, Tripura borders the Indian states of Assam and Mizoram. This geographical encirclement by Bangladesh (formerly East Pakistan) has profoundly shaped Tripura's demography, economy, culture, and political history. Tripura was an independent kingdom (the Manikya dynasty) before merging with India in 1949.",
      "id": "57rzmkb"
    },
